# Every request waits for the answer to the one before it, and every
# request is written 64 bytes at a time 20 ms apart, so the
# whole walk is a function of guest time and no write outruns the
# 128-byte RX FIFO. Do not hand-edit: re-run the capture and
# regenerate.
# Firmware: fw-esp32c6 esp32c6,server,radio (defaults) at 7e043ae2d, flash-backed
# Project: projects/test/shader-oracle (the host oracle's own project; clock-free, 64 LEDs on D10 = gpio18)
# Link: USB-Serial-JTAG (WALK_LINK=usb), host attached from power-on
# Captured by scripts/emu/upload-walk.sh over a real lp-cli upload (M5 P4); request 11 (projectRead) waits for the compile line, chunks 20 ms apart, for the reasons walks/README.md gives

after "[RECOVERY] boot complete (first frame served)" "M!{\"id\":18446744073709551615,\"msg\":\"hello\"}\n"
