after "\"id\":1," "M!{\"id\":2,\"msg\":{\"filesystem\":{\"write\":{\"path\":\"/projects/Shader"
then +20ms " oracle/README.md\",\"data\":\"# shader-oracle\\n\\nA project whose on"
then +20ms "ly job is to render **the same bytes everywhere**, so a\\ndevice'"
then +20ms "s output can be diffed against a host's instead of admired.\\n\\nI"
then +20ms "t is the fixture for `lp-app/lpa-server/tests/shader_oracle_fram"
then +20ms "e.rs` and\\n`scripts/m4-hardware-walk.sh`. It is not a demo \xe2\x80\x94 i"
then +20ms "t is deliberately plain to\\nlook at and deliberately awkward to "
then +20ms "change.\\n\\n## The four constraints, and what breaks if you relax"
then +20ms " one\\n\\n**No clock, and no `time` input.** Every frame is identi"
then +20ms "cal, so a host render\\nand a device render can be compared witho"
then +20ms "ut synchronising anything. Add a time\\ninput and the comparison "
then +20ms "needs the two sides to agree on *when*, which they\\nnever will.\\"
then +20ms "n\\n**Exactly 64 LEDs.** The device-side readout caps its one-sho"
then +20ms "t hex dump at\\n`MAX_DUMP_LEDS` \xe2\x80\x94 64, in\\n`lp-fw/fw-esp32s3/src"
then +20ms "/output/rmt/frame_dump.rs`. At exactly 64 the dump is the\\n*whol"
then +20ms "e* frame, so the comparison covers every byte. Make the fixture "
then +20ms "bigger and\\nthe diff silently becomes a prefix check \xe2\x80\x94 passing"
then +20ms " while the untested tail\\ndiverges. The host test transcribes th"
then +20ms "e same constant, so raising the fixture\\nmeans raising both.\\n\\n"
then +20ms "**A neutral output pipeline.** `output.json` sets `white_point ["
then +20ms "1,1,1]`,\\n`brightness 1`, and LUT, dithering and interpolation a"
then +20ms "ll off. Under exactly that\\nconfiguration `DisplayPipeline` coll"
then +20ms "apses to a stateless `(v + 0x80) >> 8`, so\\nthe bytes on the wir"
then +20ms "e are the engine's samples and nothing else. Turn dithering\\nor "
then +20ms "interpolation on and the pipeline becomes *temporal*: the same i"
then +20ms "nput yields\\ndifferent bytes depending on frame history, and the"
then +20ms " oracle stops describing the\\ndevice.\\n\\n**A shader that is hard"
then +20ms " to get accidentally right.** `shader.glsl` reaches for a\\ndivid"
then +20ms "e, a square root, a two-argument arctan, transcendentals through"
then +20ms " the\\nbuiltin table, a data-dependent branch, and a helper call."
then +20ms " A pattern of flat\\nramps would render plausibly through a half-"
then +20ms "broken backend; this one does not.\\n\\n## Running it\\n\\n```bash\\n"
then +20ms "cargo test -p lpa-server --test shader_oracle_frame -- --nocaptu"
then +20ms "re\\nscripts/m4-hardware-walk.sh            # flash an ESP32-S3, "
then +20ms "push, render, compare\\n```\\n\\nThe walk flashes `just flash-fw-es"
then +20ms "p32s3 <port> frame-dump`. The RMT driver now\\ndrives real LEDs, "
then +20ms "and an LED cannot be diffed; `frame-dump` is the opt-in\\nfeature"
then +20ms " that also prints each transmitted frame as `[OUT] dump \xe2\x80\xa6` / `"
then +20ms "[OUT]\\nframe \xe2\x80\xa6`. A default build renders exactly the same byte"
then +20ms "s and says nothing about\\nthem, so the walk would report \\\"nothi"
then +20ms "ng rendered\\\".\\n\\nThe test prints two transcripts. `[ORACLE]` is"
then +20ms " wasmtime; `[ORACLE-RV32]` is\\n`lpvm-native`'s rv32 emulation \xe2\x80"
then +20ms "\x94 the same code generator firmware JITs, one ISA\\nover. Which of"
then +20ms " the two a device agrees with is the diagnosis, not a detail:\\ns"
then +20ms "ee `docs/defects/2026-07-30-q32-native-vs-wasmtime-last-bit.md`,"
then +20ms " where the\\ndistinction was the difference between \\\"the Xtensa "
then +20ms "backend is broken\\\" and \\\"the\\nnative and WASM engines have alwa"
then +20ms "ys differed in the last bit\\\".\\n\\n## Known-good\\n\\n2026-07-30, E"
then +20ms "SP32-S3 (XIAO ESP32-S3 Plus, rev v0.2), `fw-esp32s3` with\\n`node"
then +20ms "-shader` + `node-fixture`: **192 of 192 bytes identical** to bot"
then +20ms "h host\\nengines, `crc=0x55772254`, compiled on device in 63 ms.\\"
then +20ms "n\"}}}}\n"
